          "Description": {
            "TableId": "/Game/UI/JournalData/Entries/ST_JournalEntries.ST_JournalEntries",
            "Key": "BunnyCactusSeed",
            "SourceString": "The bunny cactus isn't only named that way because of its rabbit-ear-like limbs. It's also a prolific reproducer. A single plant can produce dozens of seeds, and in turn it can create dozens of bunny cacti. \r\n\r\nNow I think of it, the bunny cactus also develops little tufts of fur on its spikes, reminiscent of a rabbit's cotton tail. Damn, they really nailed the naming of this cactus.",
